<HEAD><style>/* Classic Editorial — identity is hierarchy, spacing, grid, and proportion. Every value below
   is a theme variable; nothing depends on a face, a hue, or a texture. */
.gml-card {
  --hairline: var(--neutral-border-color);
  --grid-divider-color: var(--hairline);
  --grid-divider-width: 1px;
}

/* 1 · Kicker over a hairline: the tracked-caps eyebrow carries its own full-width hairline as a
   bottom border, so the pair is one node and the heading below keeps the native eyebrow hug.
   Dose: one per card, top of the column it introduces. */
.kicker.gml-paragraph { padding-bottom: 7pt; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); margin-block-end: 10pt; }
/* Heavy rule: the masthead / act-break register in heading ink. Dose: covers, dividers, closing. */
.heavy.gml-divider { --divider-color: var(--heading-color); --divider-thickness: 2pt; border-radius: 0; }

/* 2 · Stat rail and metric: tabular figures so stacked numbers align; the gloss hugs its figure. */
.metric { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums; }
.metric h2.gml-heading, .metric h3.gml-heading, .metric .gml-title { letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
.gloss.gml-paragraph { margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap) * 0.3); }
/* Inside a metric rail the gloss sits directly under its figure: the figure's own descent supplies the air. */
.metric .gloss.gml-paragraph { margin-block-start: 0; }

/* Column takeaway under a metric rail: the concluding claim stands off from the last ruled row by
   more than the rows keep between themselves, so it reads as the column's conclusion rather than a fourth figure. */
.claim.gml-paragraph { margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap) * 2.5); }

/* 3 · Two-column measure: sustained prose at 55–70 characters per line, ragged right, no seam. */
.prose p.gml-paragraph { text-wrap: pretty; hyphens: manual; }
.measure { max-width: 520pt; }
/* Masthead headline (cover, closing): nine columns, so a 60-character headline wraps to two lines. */
.measure.wide { max-width: 660pt; text-wrap: balance; }

/* 5 · Accent quote glyph and quote voice: one oversized opening mark set as a display node beside
   the quote; the quote itself reads in the heading voice with no bar. */
.quote.gml-title { line-height: 0.6; margin-block-end: 0; }
.quote.gml-blockquote { padding-inline-start: 0; }
.quote.gml-blockquote > .gml-blockquote__bar { display: none; }
.quote.gml-blockquote p.gml-paragraph { font-family: var(--heading-font); font-weight: var(--heading-font-weight); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }

/* 6 · Figure caption grammar: a semibold lead-in, a muted sentence, then a credit/source line. */
.source.gml-paragraph { margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap) * 0.45); }

/* 7 · Ruled ledger: caps header over a heavy rule, hairlines between rows, numerals right-set. */
.ledger { --table-border-color: var(--hairline); --table-border-width: 1px; --table-header-color: var(--heading-color); --table-header-weight: 600; --table-cell-padding: 12pt 12pt 12pt 0; --table-radius: 0; }
.ledger .gml-table__row[data-header] .gml-table__cell { border-bottom: 2pt solid var(--heading-color); letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: calc(11 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); }
.ledger .gml-table__cell:not([data-col='0']) { text-align: end; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.ledger .gml-table__row:last-child .gml-table__cell { border-bottom: var(--table-border-width) solid var(--table-border-color); }

/* 8 · Numbered column head: a light large numeral over a hairline, drawn by the grid marker so it
   renumbers on reorder. Dose: peer columns and steps. */
.tick .gml-grid-cell { --marker-color: var(--heading-color); --marker-font-weight: 300; --marker-font-size: calc(var(--role-display-md-pt, 52) * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); --marker-rule-color: var(--hairline); --marker-rule-thickness: 1px; }

/* Contents rows: muted inline ordinals in a narrow gutter. */
.toc .gml-grid-cell { --marker-color: var(--body-color-muted); --marker-font-weight: 400; --marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 10pt; }

/* Photographic plates keep square corners — the register has no rounded frames. A caption or name
   set under an in-flow plate keeps a clear line of air from the crop (≥14pt). */
.plate .gml-figure, .plate .gml-figure__img { border-radius: 0; }
.plate .gloss.gml-paragraph, .plate h4.gml-heading { margin-block-start: 15pt; }
/* People cells: the role line hugs its name (6pt) and the credit sentence stands off from the role (16pt),
   so name+role read as one group and the sentence as the next. */
.plate .meta.gml-paragraph { margin-block-start: -5pt; margin-block-end: 7pt; }

/* Cover metadata (byline, date, folio-style credits): tracked caps at caption size. */
.cover-meta.gml-paragraph { letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }

/* Icon chips on the icon-led list: one outlined circle treatment, an outlined circle over each column head. */
.chips .gml-grid-cell { --marker-border-color: var(--heading-color); --marker-border-width: 1px; --marker-color: var(--heading-color); --marker-gap: 10pt; }</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="6ushZY_0Zd"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="TP5WlI_ukD"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">MEDIA EVOLUTION · VISUAL COMMUNICATION</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><display size="lg" class="measure wide">The grid learns to move</display><p font-size="20pt" class="measure">The page changes from a fixed instance, to a coded interactive state, to generated variation.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Print</h4><p font-size="17pt">Fixed instance</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Digital</h4><p font-size="17pt">Coded state</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Computational</h4><p font-size="17pt">Generated variation</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><p role="caption" class="cover-meta">THESIS · WHEN A MEDIUM CHANGES, PRODUCTION, DISTRIBUTION, INTERACTION, AND AUTHORSHIP ARE REORGANIZED—NOT AUTOMATICALLY IMPROVED.</p><hr class="heavy"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="jBqINRC3zm"><grid divider="sm neutral-border"><grid-item id="9s7iVRP-Jc" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">A WORKING DEFINITION</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><h1>A medium is a system</h1><p font-size="18pt">Tools, infrastructure, interfaces, and conventions act on one another. Change one component and the others come under pressure.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption"><b>Example:</b> a browser-readable format enables linked interfaces; network infrastructure circulates them; repeated use establishes new conventions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="VB7LaP1mxK" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><smart-layout variant="cycle" cell-size="20"><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/5B6i5D877HhdTptwsV8NJQ.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon"></icon><div><h4>Tools and formats</h4><p font-size="17pt">Define what can be made.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/gEfcKBPruKx1cEXelEfF.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon"></icon><div><h4>Infrastructure</h4><p font-size="17pt">Carries and preserves it.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/9ouIQHYODGMzf0CAm1BR.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon"></icon><div><h4>Interfaces</h4><p font-size="17pt">Expose possible actions.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/b9cAMkUS6R5F5mSXxYQ9.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon"></icon><div><h4>Conventions</h4><p font-size="17pt">Shape expected behavior.</p></div></smart-layout-item></smart-layout></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="08_LI7nOXR" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="uc0ka6ai31" class="plate" padding="0" colspan="34"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Y6LAGzNcT9qISSC_hwji2.png" saved-media-id="kezdffdpg3vttaq" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="documentary-feature" alt="Documentary-style conceptual image inside a contemporary letterpress shop, showing a printer arranging movable type in a forme" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"></grid-item><grid-item id="nIRZEao4R7" class="prose" colspan="26"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">PRINT CIVILIZATION</p><h2>Print stabilizes space</h2><p font-size="18pt">Type, margins, sequence, and edition become repeatable spatial decisions. Revision largely precedes circulation; the reader encounters a resolved arrangement.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 0" class="toc"><grid-item id="Ma_Lb7IUDa"><h4>Select and space units</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="025ra8Po8k"><h4>Lock the composition into a forme</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="DYZB5ta3aw"><h4>Repeat the arrangement across impressions</h4></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption" class="source">Generated view of a contemporary letterpress workshop; conceptual process illustration, not an archival artifact or historical reproduction.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-FNfapk_vG"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Fsi9VAhGBV"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">DIGITAL ERA · DOCUMENTED MILESTONES</p><h2>The document joins a network</h2><p font-size="18pt" class="measure">The page becomes addressable, linkable, updateable, and connected to user action. Publishing shifts from distributing finished copies to maintaining networked versions.</p><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="5bN_NkahG2" colspan="38"><table col-widths="[24,76]" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p role="eyebrow">1989</p></td><td><h4>Tim Berners-Lee proposes the Web at CERN.</h4></td></tr><tr><td><p role="eyebrow">30 APRIL 1993</p></td><td><h4>CERN places Web software in the public domain.</h4></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="TdV-sYo56C" class="prose" background-color="surface" colspan="22"><p role="eyebrow">THE CHANGED RELATIONSHIP</p><h3>From reader to user</h3><p font-size="18pt">A coded state can respond, link elsewhere, and change after publication. The designer structures pathways and behavior as well as composition.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption" class="source">Source: <a href="https://home.cern/science/computing/the-birth-of-the-web/">CERN, “The birth of the Web”</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="RpWjBRqe-F"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Dmeqb-n5Cj"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">COMPARATIVE LENS</p><h2>What changes across the three eras?</h2><table col-widths="[22,26,26,26]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="ledger"><tbody><tr><td><p>Dimension</p></td><td><p>Print</p></td><td><p>Digital</p></td><td><p>Computational</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Production</b></p></td><td><p>Composed fixed instance</p></td><td><p>Maintained coded state</p></td><td><p>Generated variation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Distribution</b></p></td><td><p>Editions</p></td><td><p>Network access</p></td><td><p>On-demand synthesis</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Audience</b></p></td><td><p>Reader</p></td><td><p>User</p></td><td><p>Participant and evaluator</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Authorship</b></p></td><td><p>Visible makers</p></td><td><p>Collaborative stacks</p></td><td><p>People, data, models, and interfaces</p></td></tr></tbody></table><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption" class="source">Dominant tendencies, not sealed eras: each newer system carries older forms inside it.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="eAdq1zG09V"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="IMAvnOaHi7"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">AGE OF COMPUTATIONAL INTELLIGENCE</p><h2>One set of conditions can produce many outputs</h2><p font-size="18pt" class="measure">The designer increasingly specifies a system, evaluates its variations, and revises the conditions for the next run.</p><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="4IK8oqE4H4" cell-style="outline" colspan="14"><p role="eyebrow">1 · CONDITIONS</p><h3>Intent + constraints</h3><p font-size="17pt">Brief, data, rules, or prompt.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Pg3qc0Gzot" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="3"><p font-size="24pt" align="center">→</p></grid-item><grid-item id="2ZaDgVChwu" background-color="accent" colspan="13"><p role="eyebrow">2 · COMPUTATION</p><h3>Model</h3><p font-size="17pt">Transforms inputs according to learned or encoded relationships.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="khDKmlk7Rb" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="3"><p font-size="24pt" align="center">→</p></grid-item><grid-item id="e3UEXpqCFe" colspan="27"><p role="eyebrow">3 · ILLUSTRATIVE VARIATIONS</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="7pt 10pt"><grid-item id="eDFi_Ujyaa" cell-style="subtle"><h4>Condensed output</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="lExoI1ylQ2" cell-style="subtle"><h4>Expanded output</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="adI5o00Lik" cell-style="subtle"><h4>Reframed output</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="t6a7hdkynA" background-color="surface" padding="11pt 14pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">4 · HUMAN JUDGMENT</p><h4>Compare fitness, bias, provenance, and consequence.</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="XEJoDl-qp-" background-color="surface" padding="11pt 14pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">5 · REVISION ↩</p><h4>Change the conditions, document the decision, and run again.</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VtUmZ_XYjR"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="0_kcBlBYYr"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">TRADE-OFFS, NOT DESTINY</p><h2>New media contain older logics</h2><p font-size="18pt" class="measure">Media accumulate rather than replace one another. Each layer adds capacities and dependencies while retaining parts of the systems beneath it.</p><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="LPMS2xEtRY" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><diagram template-key="concentric_circles" align="center" width="500pt" height="275pt" data-meta="{&quot;step&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Print</h4><p>Composition; stable instances</p>&quot;,&quot;icon&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/_app_static/icons/v0/newspaper.svg&quot;,&quot;tempUrl&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;meta&quot;:{&quot;height&quot;:512,&quot;width&quot;:512},&quot;query&quot;:&quot;newspaper&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.icon&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;done&quot;,&quot;uploadStatus&quot;:3}},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Digital</h4><p>Networked state; interaction</p>&quot;,&quot;icon&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/_app_static/icons/v0/chart-network.svg&quot;,&quot;tempUrl&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;meta&quot;:{&quot;height&quot;:512,&quot;width&quot;:640},&quot;query&quot;:&quot;network&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.icon&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;done&quot;,&quot;uploadStatus&quot;:3}},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Computational</h4><p>Generation and evaluation</p>&quot;,&quot;icon&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/_app_static/icons/v0/server.svg&quot;,&quot;tempUrl&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;meta&quot;:{&quot;height&quot;:512,&quot;width&quot;:512},&quot;query&quot;:&quot;cpu&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.icon&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;done&quot;,&quot;uploadStatus&quot;:3}}],&quot;colorScheme&quot;:&quot;monochrome&quot;}"></diagram><p role="caption">Conceptual model of dominant tendencies; the eras overlap and do not form a hierarchy of quality.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Ic_gJgWsza" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">A CONTEMPORARY ARTIFACT</p><h3>A generative poster contains all three</h3><grid divider="sm neutral-border" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 0"><grid-item id="iiZC9Dww8K"><p role="eyebrow">PRINT LOGIC</p><p font-size="17pt">Hierarchy, type, image, margin, and edition.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UXXI9PBogn"><p role="eyebrow">DIGITAL LOGIC</p><p font-size="17pt">A coded file is revised, linked, and distributed through a network.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MuKDbXLiSa"><p role="eyebrow">COMPUTATIONAL LOGIC</p><p font-size="17pt">Rules or models produce variations that require selection and evaluation.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="vI9JNh84E4"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="IDaMx_sPZa"><p role="eyebrow" class="kicker">A METHOD FOR PRACTICE</p><h2>Design the conditions, not only the artifact</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="RFg_sLHoZC" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">READ ANY MEDIUM THROUGH FIVE QUESTIONS</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 0" class="toc"><grid-item id="tFaeBQ-0tr"><h4>What is fixed, and what can vary?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="Cl9t_ywvXG"><h4>Who can make, publish, revise, and respond?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="gZhuJaF9cb"><h4>How does the work travel and persist?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="_eiIuXZy1N"><h4>Where are decisions visible or hidden?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="fxxgtGr_ir"><h4>What role does the interface give its audience?</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="9s3w1o9r8N" background-color="surface" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">FINAL STUDIO BRIEF</p><h2 font-size="30pt">One message.<br>Three systems.</h2><p font-size="17pt">Keep the intent constant. Translate it across:</p><ul><li><b>Print:</b> a fixed composition</li><li><b>Interactive:</b> a responsive state</li><li><b>Generative:</b> a variable system</li></ul><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><hr class="heavy"><p role="caption">Document how production, distribution, interaction, and authorship change. Evaluate changed roles—not only changed appearance.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>